#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:187
#: c7636719f4114f9fb92b514e80578a58
msgid "Each switch position can be assigned to a script function. This means that you can script up to six different camera controls such as triggering the shutter and setting different levels of zoom. For this tutorial, we'll show you how to set up three functions using only the first channel, but this process can be followed to utilize the full six options if you choose to."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:195
#: 9d5a89e7df8e41fdb42e97a35e67ad43
msgid "Configuring the CHDK cable for use with ArduPilot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:197
#: 9b6d0532e78348cfa9d576617a6bf016
msgid "First we need to select an RC channel to assign to CHDK's channel 1. Connect your plane's autopilot to Mission Planner. Go to **Configuration \\| Radio Calibration** to locate an available channel and its corresponding three-position switch on your RC transmitter. For this tutorial, we'll use channel 7. (If you decide to use a different channel, substitute your channel wherever we input channel 7.) Don't disconnect your autopilot yet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:205
#: c26941683b9742b087328307c0a75677
msgid "Before we fly, we'll need to test the integration between this channel and the CHDK cable by manually changing the switch position and observing the result. In order to allow manual control of this channel, we need to change an important parameter in Mission Planner. Under **Configuration \\| Standard Parameters**, scroll about 4/5 of the way down to find the **Servo out function** parameters for each channel. Find the parameter that corresponds to your camera control channel. For us, it's **Servo out function (SERVO7_FUNCTION or RC7_FUNCTION)**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:216
#: d11756a2b1b041feae9d71ba7426b355
msgid "Set this parameter to **Manual** whenever you want to control your camera using your RC transmitter; set to **Disabled** when you want the autopilot to control the camera automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:220
#: e083a3d2c8744ccaa79fb458e3dee788
msgid "Since we're using the RC transmitter to test the CHDK cable, set **Servo out function** to **Manual**. Select **Write Params** before disconnecting your autopilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:224
#: 2e4f1e7ab0d64ddd9eb0edcec99cfd10
msgid "Once you've chosen your camera control channel, you'll need to connect your CHDK cable to the autopilot's output pins. Connect either of the pin connectors on the CHDK cable to the autopilot output pins corresponding to your camera control channel (black cable on the outside). For example, we connected our CHDK cable to the channel 7 output pins on the autopilot. Make sure no input pins are connected to the autopilot for that channel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:231
#: cd1f446298b24150b7edf7c38571caa8
msgid "For **Pixhawk**, connect the CHDK cable to aux out pin 5. However, this pin outputs only 3.3V, and 5V are required to trigger CHDK. To convert to 5V, you'll need to integrate a step-up converter (`like the one here from Sparkfun <https://www.sparkfun.com/products/10968>`__) in-line with the cable to trigger CHDK."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:237
#: f986b11c6eb6406fa72fb824058cf21c
msgid "Adding a script"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:239
#: 8c9c1390302e462d955881ff4bb1ff1e
msgid "Now that you've configured your CHDK cable, we'll add a script to control the camera when commanded by the autopilot. Let's break down a CHDK cable UBASIC script into its main parts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:252
#: c02e46fca21f40989c9b62b6bae9f7bd
msgid "This section defines the parameters that will be used later by the functions. **@param** names the parameter with a variable and a phrase; **@default** specifies its value. These three parameters specify zoom levels, so if you wanted to change a zoom level, you could easily do so by entering a new value after the variable following **@default**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:274
#: 4bce206740ec490a8c481202de5f9d63
msgid "This is the main body of the script. It tells CHDK to read the power pulse from the USB port (**get_usb_power**) and, according to what range it falls under, execute a specific function. The values here are listed in centiseconds, which is why they differ from the table shown above (5 centiseconds = 50 milliseconds)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:310
#: 9e6649aac1264e2f84c476a49d43fcd9
msgid "This is where the script defines what each function will do. Since we aren't utilizing the channel 2 options, **ch2up**, **ch2mid**, and **ch2down** functions are empty. The **ch1up** function will set the zoom to the value specified by the variable **s** using the **set_zoom** command and take a picture using the **shoot** command. The **ch1mid** function uses **set_zoom** to set the lens to its stowed position, and the **ch1down** function fully extends the lens. The **print** command will output the specified text to the camera's display along with the actual output value of the USB power pulse (**k**)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:320
#: e5a2aabde90c4c3d8e1ae8a53af5d48a
msgid "In short, the above script will cause the following behaviors:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:322
#: 26bbad4414b74105b91c6639c97f585d
msgid "When channel 7 is set to the up position, CHDK will set zoom to 10 and take a picture."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:325
#: af79fa60664543e68abc9287bd5a7fcb
msgid "When channel 7 is set to the mid position, CHDK will set zoom to 30 (stowed position)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:328
#: f65dcd2284bd4480a2f7da8b01c3c9c2
msgid "When channel 7 is set to the down position, CHDK will set zoom to 100 (extended position)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:331
#: 661a2728c0974091ab3e6ffc67ea443f
msgid "`Click here to view the above script <https://download.ardupilot.org/downloads/wiki/other_files/3DR_Shoot.txt>`__, copy into a text editor, and save as \\ **3DR_Shoot.bas**. Now that you're familiar with how the script works, you can easily change the commands of each function. For example, you can add a **shoot** command to **ch1down** or change one of the zoom level parameters. If you're utilizing the channel two functions, you can easily add commands to those functions in the same format shown above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:339
#: 614b756565a644c9801c325cfce5f4c5
msgid "Add the script file to the SD card as described in the previous section."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:342
#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:622
#: c2d11e865f8f4d649cbb365adb712cab
#: e905a79d4df043a1af4ca136bdb57e1b
msgid "Testing the CHDK cable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:344
#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:624
#: c0f216e0f9264a81bc726bfde0e9be1d
#: 90513af0e6504f8eb2ab0f6ea4ea7fb1
msgid "Testing the CHDK cable will ensure that our camera controls execute as expected and is a great opportunity to test for potential noise created by your equipment setup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:351
#: 4c0d72d84a3c44cd8db11033b965a5a0
msgid "To tell CHDK to listen to the cable, we need to set the Enable Remote parameter. On the camera, access the CHDK menu, select **Remote Parameters,** and select **Enable Remote** as shown. This setting must be enabled to allow communication with the CHDK cable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:356
#: 08b71cd79bef47008b8b172f55387f18
msgid "Connect the CHDK cable to the camera's USB port, and run \\ **3DR_Shoot.bas**. Test the result of each switch position. The resulting behaviors should reflect those listed in the previous step. Observe the USB pulse values output to the camera display, and compare them with the ranges show in the code. If you encounter problems, see the **Advanced Topics**\\ section below for additional testing and troubleshooting information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:365
#: 79f067347df748fca73a4aa613c16bc3
msgid "Programming camera controls in Mission Planner"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:367
#: 1ae7fb51347c48c8a01bd066a9a67b21
msgid "Mission Planner allows you to program servo outputs as events at waypoints. By using this feature, we can add a command to output a PWM value (corresponding to a switch position and function) after the plane achieves each waypoint."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:372
#: 404ebaba33604fabb7ce44bdfd246c16
msgid "Once you have your waypoints configured in Mission Planner as shown below, select your first waypoint and click “Add Below”."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:378
#: 7c3708d6df8c4a6ab5fe3b8edc9e5c8b
msgid "For your new command, set **Command** type to **DO_SET_SERVO**. (This tells the autopilot that this command means output to a servo.) Set **Ser No**\\ (servo number) to the number of your camera control channel (ex:**7**). (This tells the autopilot where to output: for us, servo channel 7 is the CHDK cable.) And set **PWM** to **1900**. (This value tells the autopilot what to output: 1,900 microseconds of pulse width modulation corresponds to the high position under which the shoot command is located). Repeat this process for each waypoint at which you would like to take a picture. The screen below shows a shutter command correctly applied at each of three waypoints."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:394
#: 3e3b7dbef1c245888e42e9f93410617a
msgid "Columns in the Waypoints table accrue different meanings based on the type of command currently selected. These column definitions only become visible when the command is selected as different parameters apply to different types of commands.*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:399
#: a471a6a0bf634e768cb9b86199af90df
msgid "Since we're using the autopilot to control the camera, we need to set the \\ **Servo out function (RC7_FUNCTION or SERVO7_FUNCTION)** parameter to **Disabled** (under **Standard Parameters**). Write waypoints and parameters to the autopilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:404
#: ba60291b644a452a8866ee5495e8006f
msgid "Ensure that your camera and autopilot are connected correctly. Run \\ **3DR_Shoot.bas** prior to launch. Fly your mission according to standard practices and safety procedures."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:409
#: 25c506b0f6174c5ca4c3a3a71edd4442
msgid "Creating a composite image"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:411
#: 0b2ff0f6b5a248daa360396d60c91086
msgid "One of our favorite applications of CHDK is creating a map of an area by stitching automatically-captured pictures into a composite image. We'll use the same `3DR_Shoot.bas <https://download.ardupilot.org/downloads/wiki/other_files/3DR_Shoot.txt>`__\\ script that we used in the previous section. The process is similar to setting shutter triggers at waypoints, only to make sure we capture the entire area we need more frequent, more regular waypoints. We’ll do this automatically using Mission Planner’s **Grid V2** automatic waypoint function."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:422
#: 681de5a5ac63404fbdbcf6adaa22886e
msgid "Setting waypoints with GridV2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:424
#: 0059c529cb4f4b68a19435f3b8046c92
msgid "First locate the area you wish to map in Mission Planner. Right-click and select \\ **Draw Polygon\\| Add Polygon Point**. Add polygon points until you have created a polygon around the area you wish to map. Once you are satisfied with your polygon, right-click and select **Auto WP \\| GridV2** as shown below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:433
#: f9311437f4a04ee088a5036ac7255084
msgid "Input a relative altitude (100 feet is fine if you are unsure). Input a distance between lines; the larger the number, the fewer waypoints you’ll end up with. When prompted, enter a distance between each waypoint; the same rationale applies here. Enter line direction; the waypoints below show a line direction of 70. When prompted to add camera triggers, input “Yes”; *this will create a command after each waypoint, it will not automatically set up your CHDK commands*. We recommend experimenting with these settings until you find the waypoint configuration that is right for your mission. You should now have a grid of waypoints mapped onto your polygon as shown below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:447
#: da157a4143024bfcb6ddb7d528728ffa
msgid "Here is where we have to switch our automatic functionality for some manual labor. GridV2 has created a command after each waypoint with command type DO_DIGICAM_CONTROL. However, for our CHDK setup, we need command type **DO_SET_SERVO**. For each DO_DIGICAM_CONTROL command, change command type to \\ **DO_SET_SERVO**, set **Ser No** to **7** (or whichever channel you're using), and set **PWM** to **1,100** (to call the 3DR_Shoot.bas function that takes a picture)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:455
#: 6fab40b5bbba48c593eda67a155df2f1
msgid "When run, this mission returns a set of images that can be stitched together to create a map of the selected polygon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:459
#: c8aad96b81a5465293b8c9366a67a51f
msgid "Stitching images"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:461
#: 8a74143b202f4cc5b3e7d426253d1bef
msgid "`Microsoft Image Composite Editor (ICE) <http://research.microsoft.com/en-us/um/redmond/projects/ice/>`__ is a great, free tool for automatically stitching images together into a composite. Just upload your images, and ICE will stitch them together. Here's an example of one of our composites:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:469
#: a50ab12a37b4421dbe8e0d2c51c3d172
msgid "We hope this solution provides some enhanced functionality to your missions and expands your autonomous imaging capabilities. For more information, check out the Advanced Topics section below."
msgstr ""

