#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:555
#: 76884467536a40b8b656dfbb4f40673b
msgid "CHDK cables work by translating pulse width modulation (PWM) output by the autopilot into USB power pulses that can be read by the camera. It does this by establishing a range of how long power is applied to the USB port (ex: 40-80 ms) and assigning that range to a PWM value corresponding to a channel switch position (ex: Channel middle).The table below shows the corresponding output values between the switch position on the RC transmitter, the autopilot's PWM output, and the camera's USB power. In practice, our Spektrum DX 8 outputs the values shown in the rightmost column."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:566
#: cb5d33de8a074acdad69a322ee7fb261
msgid "Spektrum DX8 USB power readings (ms)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:568
#: 7cb84fc026e143ccb330e99d4509267a
msgid "30"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:570
#: eec5681010374500a05e173fc55552d0
msgid "50 or 60"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:572
#: d4cd7682e089498f8c335fda3fee3661
msgid "90"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:574
#: bf51b1f2c9b74b598eea493686564d13
msgid "130"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:576
#: 4078fb91b18d4c30ac495312130725fb
msgid "150 or 160"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:578
#: 3d23f5da4af648d8ae317c206bd2911f
msgid "190"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:581
#: 881722e29db74e39b3b3825dd45143e0
msgid "To verify that your transmitter behaves similarly, you may want to perform a test to ensure that a valid USB power value is returned for each switch position. View the `3DR CHDK Tester script here <https://download.ardupilot.org/downloads/wiki/other_files/3DRCHDKTester.txt>`__. Copy the contents into a text editor and save as **3DRCHDKTester.bas**. Load into your (unlocked) SD card by copying the file into the **Scripts** folder (in the **CHDK** folder)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:589
#: c79e2ddcc88f434a8a3c2116cadecf12
msgid "Configuring CHDK cable for Testing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:591
#: 9cded9cff6074f948f774a011038501e
msgid "Before we can test the CHDK cable, we'll need to choose a channel for camera control and configure the corresponding inputs. Connect your plane's autopilot to Mission Planner. Go to **Configuration \\| Radio Calibration** to locate an available channel and its corresponding switch on your RC transmitter. (We'll use channel 7.) Check the PWM outputs for the up, mid, and down positions of the channel. Compare them with the table shown above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:599
#: f0539598ada241afb1c0df5c4b9decb7
msgid "Before we disconnect the autopilot, we need to change an important parameter that you'll be using often. Under **Configuration** -> **Standard Parameters**, scroll about 4/5 of the way down to find the **Servo out function** parameters for each channel. Find the parameter that corresponds to your camera control channel. For us, it's **Servo out function (SERVO7_FUNCTION or RC7_FUNCTION)**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:606
#: 217e7ad0522e49b980e2330e1ee87a50
msgid "***Set this parameter to Manual whenever you want to control your camera using your RC transmitter; set to Disabled when you want the autopilot to control the camera automatically.***"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:610
#: 0fffd1f71b3e475cbb2a976a21534dd8
msgid "Since we're using the RC transmitter to test the CHDK cable, set **Servo out function** to **Manual**. Select Write Params before disconnecting your autopilot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:614
#: 0bbb7f5c4a514c31a8e6167e599a4815
msgid "Once you've chosen your camera control channel, you'll need to connect your CHDK cable to the autopilot's output pins. Connect either of the pin connectors on the CHDK cable to the autopilot output pins corresponding to your camera control channel (black cable on the outside). For example, we connected our CHDK cable to the channel 7 output pins on the autopilot. Make sure no input pins are connected for that channel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:628
#: 4ee43f3d8607494e982715caf78669f7
msgid "Connect the CHDK cable to the camera's USB port. Turn the camera on, load the \\ **3DRCHDKTester.bas** script (by selecting **Load Script from File** from the main CHDK menu), and press the shutter button to run the test script."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:633
#: 6064b23fbbd149a1b5e94f8ab347936f
msgid "To perform the test, set each camera control channel position on your RC transmitter and observe the outputs on the display. Verify that these outputs are within the acceptable USB power ranges in the table above. If you encounter problems, you may need to shield your cable to prevent noise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:640
#: a74ec2af38db46089d6d55c22a65f9ae
msgid "Shielding the cable"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:642
#: 7bca66aa60e44c8ca5d08a03bbe1e7c5
msgid "Coming soon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:645
#: c71f6a230e29442e884b1e0c4d7bf770
msgid "GeoTagging Images"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:647
#: 871fa3a0c70b45bdb10f648332c910e5
msgid "For information regarding geotagging images, more information can be found on `Sandro Beningo's step-by-step guide. <https://www.diydrones.com/profiles/blogs/geotagging-images-with-mission-planner>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:651
#: 3a4f333ae27c4c8488c1957e96714f48
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:653
#: 6465eeee81c44dae81d54f4e98c91e01
msgid "**Problem**: The tester script runs but does not display any output on the camera screen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:656
#: c9552f09a0d04d59b4101cefe80ce347
msgid "Cause 1: Do you have the parameter SERVOx_FUNCTION=1 ir RCx_FUNCTION=1 for manual override of the RC channel you are using? You can see both the PWM input and output on the **Configuration \\| Failsafes** screen in the Mission Planner."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:661
#: 6c8be8be551e4870990d9bae2bd7203a
msgid "Cause 2: Is your output rail powered? Even if you are getting the correct PWM signal out on your camera control channel, the output needs 5V DC. You can power the output rail with a jumper on JP1 as shown, which bridges the input power to the output, or by directly running power to the output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-chdk-camera-control-tutorial.rst:667
#: 12bb3ce3c1554657961fc9b572d1afe4
msgid "Cause 3: Do you have the remote enabled in CHDK? In the CHDK menus: Remote parameters > enable remote. Leave the other remote settings as is."
msgstr ""
